velo5x0-bsp local changes to the lifted igb glue (applied after patch 200)
  licence:   GPL-2.0, as the files it changes
  changes:   (1) the default external MDIO bus id becomes "vc-edge5x0-wan", the
             bus vc-edge5x0-board registers (the stock Debian kernel has no
             mdio-gpio, so upstream's "gpio-0" never exists there);
             (2) igb takes a module reference on the provider of that bus
             (try_module_get(bus->owner)) while it holds the bus, and drops
             it in igb_vc_mii_unregister(), so vc-edge5x0-board cannot be
             unloaded under a bound igb;
             (3) the external-MDIO PHY accessors refuse (WARN_ONCE, return
             -E1000_ERR_PHY) when called outside task context or with
             preemption/IRQs off: mdiobus_read/write take a mutex;
             (4) the PHY-info refresh moves from phy_info_timer (softirq) to a
             work item, phy_info_task; the timer only schedules it, and
             igb_down and igb_remove cancel it after del_timer_sync;
             (5) igb_remove unregisters the external buses after
             unregister_netdev, not before.

